w: 1.~As pants the hart for cool- ing streams, When hea- _ ted in the chase; _ So longs my soul, O God, for Thee, And Thy re- fresh- ing grace.
w: 2.~For Thee, my God, the liv- ing God, My thir- _ sty soul doth pine; _ O when shall I be- hold Thy face, Thou Ma- jes- ty Di- vine?
w: 3.~Why rest- less, why cast down, my soul? Trust God, _ Who will em- ploy _ His aid for thee, and change these sighs To thank- ful hymns of joy.
w: 4.~Why rest- less, why cast down, my soul? Hope still, _ and thou shalt sing _ The praise of Him Who is thy God, Thy health's e- ter- nal spring.
